  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have an array AAA consisting of XXX 000's, YYY 111's and ZZZ 222's.\n\nCheck if it is possible to rearrange array AAA such that Ai+Ai+1≥2A_i + A_{i + 1} \\ge 2Ai​+Ai+1​≥2 for each 1≤i&lt;∣A∣1 \\le i &lt; |A|1≤i&lt;∣A∣. Print Yes\\text{Yes}Yes or No\\text{No}No accordingly.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 333 integers XXX, YYY and ZZZ.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output Yes\\text{Yes}Yes if there is a valid rearrangement or No\\text{No}No otherwise.\n\n\nIt is allowed to print each character in either case, i.e. YES\\text{YES}YES, yes\\text{yes}yes and yES\\text{yES}yES will all be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "0≤X,Y,Z≤1000 \\le X, Y, Z \\le 1000≤X,Y,Z≤100",
      "2≤X+Y+Z2 \\le X + Y + Z2≤X+Y+Z"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 1 0\n1 1 1\n2 0 1\n5 1 1",
        "output": "No\nYes\nYes\nNo",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1: You have 111 occurrence of 000 and 111 occurrence of 111. The 222 possible arrays are [0,1][0, 1][0,1] and [1,0][1, 0][1,0], but neither satisfies the condition of A1+A2≥2A_1 + A_2 \\ge 2A1​+A2​≥2.\nTest case 2: The array [1,2,0][1, 2, 0][1,2,0] satisfies the necessary conditions."
      }
    ]
  },
